@war_conquest
title: The Eagle Over Axton
subtitle: Ending — Conquest
view-if: empire_outcome == "war_conquest"
new-page: true
set-bg: img/paper.jpg

The Commonwealth that could not defend itself did not survive the testing.

It was over more quickly than anyone had feared. An army half-loyal and underfed, a republic hollowed by crisis and division, a people too weary and too frightened to rise — against these the Empress's legions moved almost without checking, and within a season the eagle of New Axton flew over Axton Proper, over the Assembly hall where the Commonwealth had been proclaimed a lifetime before. The last government fled south, or to Ethia, or to a cell. The republic was not so much conquered as folded up and put away, as one puts away a thing that has stopped working.

The Restoration had its day of triumph. The Royalists rode home behind the legions; the Registry was reopened and the loyalty-oaths restored, save that now it was the magi, elevated as the chosen caste of the God of Magic's restored cult, who held the whip-hand over those who had once watched them. The faithful gave thanks for order. The schools taught that the long republican experiment had been an aberration, a fever, now mercifully broken.

And the people who had built the Commonwealth, who had voted in it and argued in it and never quite loved it enough to save it, learned the oldest lesson of all the failed republics: that liberty undefended is liberty surrendered, and that the bill, when it comes, is always paid in full.

